{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/395908-dark-eras-pitch-rise-of-empire","id":395908,"title":"Dark Eras Pitch: Rise of Empire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-07T00:21:13-08:00","id":395908,"title":"Dark Eras Pitch: Rise of Empire","content":"So, you may recall the Twice Arisen: should an Arisen's body be truly destroyed beyond any hope of repair, their cult may still resurrect them via a human sacrifice that will serve as their new body (bringing the memories of that identity with it)<br /> <br /> And if their cult is completely eliminated fate will transpire to bring a new cult together eventually.<br /> <br /> In the 15th Century Andes, the Incan priests hear the calling of their gods to offer up mummified sacrifices in their name. And these sacrifices rise, their gods risen from Ukhu Pacha, merged as one with the sacrifices offered. And these gods have a new word for their people, Twantinsuyu - Land of Four Quarters. A dream of an empire that would span the continent. And the faithful heed their gods.<br /> <br /> //To be clear, the Arisen are riding the economic wave of the era. They certainly don't rule the new empire, the Sapa Inca does. But their cults have influence to fan the flames and the dreams of Irem merge with the Incan cultures and memories of their new bodies//","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T06:08:08-08:00","id":396174,"title":"","content":"I really liked your idea glamourweaver!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T06:19:47-08:00","id":396212,"title":"","content":"Alright, if we're going to make another <b>Mummy</b> Era happen then we all need to band together and get on board. I'm very down with this one!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T02:23:04-08:00","id":397298,"title":"","content":"Something to note: A lot of the Twice-Risen are going to be physically children now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T01:02:02-08:00","id":401552,"title":"","content":"If the Werewolf Rome thing happens, then I can picture politics between the Camarilla of Ancient Rome and the Arisen Guilds of Ancient Egypt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T02:07:00-08:00","id":401659,"title":"","content":"Why does the werewolf thing need to happen? Requiem for Rome &amp; Fall of the Camarilla already have been published? Forsaken by Rome is explicitly the Western Roman Empire's territories; is Germany, France &amp; Spain more than Egypt.<br /> <br /> Still awesome but less relevant to your idea.<br /> <br /> But back to topic; a Twice-Arisen Incan Mummy Eta sounds incredible","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T08:31:38-08:00","id":401927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/395908-dark-eras-pitch-rise-of-empire#post395908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if their cult is completely eliminated fate will transpire to bring a new cult together eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to rain on your parade, but this really only happens if the Mummy has the Eternal Legend affinity, I reckon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T16:30:25-08:00","id":402597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/395908-dark-eras-pitch-rise-of-empire?p=401927#post401927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to rain on your parade, but this really only happens if the Mummy has the Eternal Legend affinity, I reckon.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what if the ones who have it after getting settled, start to make cults for the members of their meret and start summoning them from Duat in new bodies?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T16:44:05-08:00","id":402602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/395908-dark-eras-pitch-rise-of-empire?p=402597#post402597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what if the ones who have it after getting settled, start to make cults for the members of their meret and start summoning them from Duat in new bodies?</div> </div> </div> </div>You get a whole bunch of pissed off Shuankhsen? Unless they take a long time and build some exceptionally large cults, you're looking at rolling 2-4 dice, and failure gives you a Shuankhsen instead of a Twice-Arisen Mummy.<br /> <br /> This era is interesting, but I see it as interesting more because of its potential to be a huge blow to the world's Arisen population and a massive advance for the cause of Ammut. Large-scale attempts at making Twice-Arisen have pretty high odds of creating one of the few circumstances that permanently &quot;destroys&quot; one of the world's Arisen. For a species with no means to create more of itself, there's a huge capacity for this era to be portrayed as one of the great tragedies to ever befall Irem's diaspora.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T17:46:13-08:00","id":402660,"title":"","content":"Wow, if I wasn't sold on this already then Azahul just killed it. In the cWoD <b>Time of Judgement</b> the South American Mummy apocalypse has to do with a 'Well of Names' - like some pit where true names are inscribed along the wall. That's a great image to carry over: cults and Mummies just tossing people into it hoping to achieve some great thing, but only getting Shuankhsen in return.<br /> <br /> To think that there's Arisen in the modern day, in like China or Canada or wherever, and they all look back upon the days of Cuzco and just sigh and shake their heads, heavy with regret and pity is a great image and mood","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T17:49:02-08:00","id":402664,"title":"","content":"Given that apparently children's bodies are being used, I like the idea of rabid, fanged children swarming out of the pits to devour their former friends and worshippers, jaws agape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T18:04:41-08:00","id":402681,"title":"","content":"Now, that all said, I'm not sure the rise of the Incan Empire is entirely appropriate for such a setting. A time of economic prosperity and expansion doesn't really gel thematically with the kind of chaos that would be unfolding as beings who have existed for thousands of years have their very being sundered apart and are driven by their empty, never-ending hunger to turn on those they once called friends.<br /> <br /> Unless, of course, the point is to put the Shuankhsen in the position of power and play upon the sharp dichotomy between supernatural tragedy and a mortal golden age. The fear and shame and revulsion the Arisen feel as the Incan Empire advances towards its height at the behest of corrupted slaves of the Devourer, while the rightful heirs to Irem are forced to watch from the shadow and wonder if maybe, just maybe, the Devourer is better at this whole civilisation thing than they are.<br /> <br /> Really, this kind of tragedy could unfold anywhere, anytime, a widespread attempt was made to become Twice-Arisen. My automatic instinct is that a more cataclysmic time period would be more appropriate, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T06:01:05-08:00","id":403228,"title":"","content":"I thought a more interesting use of South America would be the Brazilian Gold Rush of the 1700s and the search for El Dorado. You'd have the beginnings of the Arisen class divide in Rio and the pulpy elements of looking for fabled cities of gold.<br /> <br /> Granted, I'm biased because I'm running a game just like that with my fiancee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T06:25:14-08:00","id":403241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/395908-dark-eras-pitch-rise-of-empire?p=403228#post403228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought a more interesting use of South America would be the Brazilian Gold Rush of the 1700s and the search for El Dorado. You'd have the beginnings of the Arisen class divide in Rio and the pulpy elements of looking for fabled cities of gold.<br /> <br /> Granted, I'm biased because I'm running a game just like that with my fiancee.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a brazilian I would be very biased in voting for that setting...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T19:34:49-08:00","id":404013,"title":"","content":"We are getting an entire setting book on Rio, however, so I kind of imagine that those elements would be covered in some capacity there.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd like to see something take place in central/southern Africa. Close enough to Irem for some geographical continuity, different enough culture/aesthetics to avoid feeling like yet another Middle Eastern setting (as much as I love the Middle East as a setting). Plus, it's a part of the world and history that doesn't get covered a whole lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T06:53:20-08:00","id":404440,"title":"","content":"That's kinda why one of my first suggestions on the Kickstarter comment page was for Ethiopia <b>Mummy</b> ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T09:14:36-08:00","id":404535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/395908-dark-eras-pitch-rise-of-empire?p=403228#post403228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought a more interesting use of South America would be the Brazilian Gold Rush of the 1700s and the search for El Dorado. You'd have the beginnings of the Arisen class divide in Rio and the pulpy elements of looking for fabled cities of gold.<br /> <br /> Granted, I'm biased because I'm running a game just like that with my fiancee.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T23:06:30-08:00","id":417272,"title":"","content":"So.<br /> <br /> What complete strangers here are people willing to pool their money towards creating this Dark Era with the new reward tiers opening up tomorrow? I'd also be okay with expanding Ruins of Empire to include Deceived info or turning the Biblical <b>Hunter</b> era into a crossover Era with <b>Mummy</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T23:18:27-08:00","id":417280,"title":"","content":"I wan to wait and see exactly how they structure this thing. It depends on if there is a different price for expanding a chapter vs adding a chapter from the polls vs creating a brand new era. I'm hoping this means we get some more content for <b>all</b> of the lines now. I am very happy that the team is doing this!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T23:54:04-08:00","id":417295,"title":"","content":"I'm with Second Chances in that I'm in a &quot;Wait and see&quot; mode at the moment.<br /> <br /> And besides, Inca Mummy is pretty low on my list of eras I want for Mummy. I'd much rather find a way to swing a Mutapa Mummy, or some other non-Egypt African setting for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T00:44:21-08:00","id":417321,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see the Mutapa setting, too, but I love seeing the teasing shout-outs to <b>Mummy the Resurrection</b> in <b>the Curse</b> and just putting a <b>Mummy</b> setting in the Andes would do that for me. I know Rio is coming and is 'close enough' but still","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T00:59:43-08:00","id":417328,"title":"","content":"As someone who never played the Resurrection... yeah, Rio is &quot;close enough&quot;. More importantly, Mutapa Mummy is something I would actually <i>use</i>, rather than just read and go, &quot;Yeah, that's kinda cool&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T08:45:10-08:00","id":417575,"title":"","content":"Huh. I expected Japan to be crushing the competition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T09:02:13-08:00","id":417584,"title":"","content":"Same here, or at least going to a two-way between Samurai and Pirates. I'm pleasantly surprised at this turn of events.<br /> <br /> I have a theory about it, too. While Edo and the Golden Age of Piracy are certainly <i>interesting</i> on their own, they've attracted a romanticized ideal in several cultures that's persisted into the modern day. My thinking is that the people who care more about the romanticization than the time periods themselves are divided on Pirates vs Samurai, which should let the other, less romanticized settings accrue votes based on other factors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T12:24:46-08:00","id":417775,"title":"","content":"There seems to be a weird ratio between 'people complaining about all the Western settings' and 'people who are voting for golden age of piracy'<br /> <br /> &gt;_&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T12:29:05-08:00","id":417779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com